From the dependency-preserving logical schedule, we extract the three execution descriptors used in the subsequent optimization. The weighted logical interaction graph is
\begin{equation}
G_{\mathrm{int}}=(V,E,W),
\end{equation}
where vertices represent logical qubits and the edge weights $W_{ij}$ characterize the frequency or time-weighted interaction demand between logical qubits $i$ and $j$.

